  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, for reasons of mass, siting and design, would be harmful to the balance and symmetry of the setting of the dwellinghouse within the street scene. It would restrict the breathing space and openness at the boundary and present a massing which is uncharacteristic of the host dwelling and the surrounding area.&nbsp;The proposal is therefore contrary to:&nbsp;Paragraph 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (December, 2024);&nbsp;Policy D4 of The London Plan (March 2021);&nbsp;Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of the Local Plan (September 2024); and&nbsp;LBBD Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012).&nbsp;",
    "The proposed development for reasons of mass and siting would result in unacceptable levels of overshadowing, loss of light and overbearing which would be harmful to the amenity of neighbouring occupiers. It&nbsp;therefore constitutes unneighbourly development which would be&nbsp;contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp; (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy D6&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
